    "created_at": "2020-07-08T07:50:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-07-08T07:50:54Z",
    "body": "It's certainly _possible_ for a 304 to contain a non-matching Etag, but the cache shouldn't update the response. Whether or not the client retries the request is up to it -- but usually it will, if it still wants a response. HTTP doesn't specify it because it's pretty generic, but I could see Fetch doing so (if you can get everyone to agree).\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
